 "title": "Veteran's Service Office - JOHNSON COUNTY, NEBRASKA",
 "text": "Veteran's Service Office - JOHNSON COUNTY, NEBRASKA\nJOHNSON COUNTY, NEBRASKA\n|\n|\n|\n|\n|\nHome\nCounty Offices\nOther Links\nContacts\nCounty Boards\nVETERAN'S SERVICE OFFICE\nDuties:\n|\nKEN MANDL is the Veteran's Service Officer. This office is responsible for registering Military Discharge papers, assisting Veterans with Service Connection Disability Claims, assisting Veterans with paperwork for home loans, educational benefits, disability pensions of all types, admission into a Veteran's Home, and burial expenses. They also help to arrange transportation to VA doctor appointments in Lincoln and Omaha.\n​\n|\nOffice Hours:\n|\nHours for the Veteran's Service Office: 9:00 a.m. - 3:00 p.m., Monday - Friday\nOthers by appointment - please call 402-335-6306 for an appointment.\n​\n|\nContact Information:\n|\nMailing Address: P.O. Box 217, Tecumseh, NE 68450\nPhone Number: 402-335-6306\njohnsoncovso@johnsoncounty.ne.gov\n​\n|\nOther Links:\n|\nClick here to access other information and links for the Veteran's Service Office\n|\nJohnson County VSO\n|\nState Veteran's Office\n|\nCounty Assessor\nCounty Attorney\nCounty Clerk\nCounty Sheriff\nCounty Treasurer\nDistrict Court Clerk\nEmergency Management Agency\nHighway Superintendent\nJohnson County Extension\nRegister of Deeds\nSurveyor\nVeteran's Service Office\nZoning Administrator\nPowered by\nCreate your own unique website with customizable templates.\nGet Started",
